<title>INDIA: India IDBI Mutual money market yield at 16.68 pct.</title>
<headline>India IDBI Mutual money market yield at 16.68 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>IDBI Mutual Fund's money market scheme &quot;Call I-Nit 97&quot; opened for subscription on June 9, 1997 and the initial offer to investors closed on June 14, 1997.</p>
<p>The first Net Asset Value (NAV) of &quot;Call I-Nit 97&quot; as on July 13, 1997 was 10.128 rupees, IDBI Investment Management Company said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This translates into a yield of 16.68 percent per annum. The scheme is opening for repurchase from Tuesday the 15th July '97 at NAV plus load of 0.1 percent of NAV,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22 265 9000</p>
</text>
